description:
At Flix, we offer a dynamic work environment with competitive pay, strong growth opportunities, and a tech-driven approach to making travel more accessible, sustainable, and affordable. &nbsp;

As a Support Engineer (m/f/d) at Flix, you'll be the first point of contact for IT infrastructure requests, helping employees across the globe stay productive through reliable service desk and on-site support. &nbsp;

You'll be part of a globally distributed IT Infrastructure Support Team , within our Foundation Division, that owns and manages critical services - including the employee device lifecycle (Microsoft Intune/Autopilot), our Atlassian cloud environment, and technical event support.&nbsp;

About the Role

• Resolve employee IT requests efficiently via our ticketing system, providing a smooth and friendly support experience&nbsp;

• Manage the device lifecycle end-to-end - hardware procurement, provisioning, setup, asset tracking, and troubleshooting&nbsp;

• Support collaboration tools including Office 365, Microsoft Teams, Outlook, and OneDrive&nbsp;

• Help employees get the most out of Atlassian tools such as Jira, Confluence, and JSM

• Create and maintain knowledge-base articles and IT documentation to support self-service and team efficiency

• Build hands-on experience with device management platforms and IT infrastructure tooling

• Collaborate with colleagues across global offices, contributing to team ceremonies and cross-functional projects&nbsp;

About You

• A degree, certification, or vocational training in an IT-related field (e.g. Information Technology, Computer Science, or Information Systems)&nbsp;

• 2-4 years of experience in IT support, service desk, or technical customer support&nbsp;

• Solid working knowledge of Office 365 and standard workplace collaboration tools&nbsp;

• Comfort communicating clearly and patiently with non-technical users&nbsp;

• Curiosity and a genuine eagerness to learn new technologies and workflows&nbsp;

• Hands-on experience with Microsoft cloud technologies (Intune, Entra ID, Autopilot)&nbsp;

• Experience administering Atlassian tools (Jira, Confluence, JSM)&nbsp;

• Experience supporting employees across multiple time zones or global offices (nice to have)&nbsp;

We recognize that everyone carries a unique set of valuable skills and experiences. If you think you could have an impact even though you don't meet 100% of the requirements, we still encourage you to apply. We want to hear from you! &nbsp;

What We Offer

• Travel perks : 12 free Flix vouchers + 12 discount vouchers for friends &amp; family.&nbsp;

• Work from (M)Anywhere : Depending on your role, work from another location for up to 60 days per year.&nbsp;

• Hybrid work model : We are an office-first company, but we offer flexibility to balance work and life.&nbsp;

• Wellbeing support : Access confidential 1:1 counselling, courses, and stress management for yourself and up to four family members.&nbsp;

• Learning &amp; Development : Take advantage of language classes, training courses, and expert-led sessions to grow your skills.&nbsp;

• Mentoring Program : Connect with experienced colleagues to gain insights and accelerate your career.&nbsp;

To view more local benefits specific to each office location, please check out this link: &nbsp; Locations - Flix Career

Why Join Flix?

At Flix, you’ll find teams that rally together to overcome challenges and spark creativity. We believe in ownership culture - giving you the freedom to take initiative, make an impact, and shape your own career path.
As we continue to expand across the globe, you can make a real difference in how we work.

If you’re ready to grow and lead your journey, Flix is the place for you!&nbsp;

